QUEUE, STACK, DEQUE, ARRAYDEQUE

1. Queue
- Interface
- Follows FIFO (First In First Out)
- First inserted element is removed first

Example:
Queue<Integer> q = new LinkedList<>();

Main Methods:
offer() -> insert
poll()  -> remove front
peek()  -> view front

----------------------------------------

2. Stack
- Class
- Follows LIFO (Last In First Out)
- Last inserted element is removed first

Example:
Stack<Integer> stack = new Stack<>();

Main Methods:
push() -> insert
pop()  -> remove top
peek() -> view top

----------------------------------------

3. Deque (Double Ended Queue)
- Interface
- Allows insertion/removal from both ends
- Can behave as both Queue and Stack

Example:
Deque<Integer> dq;

Main Methods:
addFirst()
addLast()
removeFirst()
removeLast()

----------------------------------------

4. ArrayDeque
- Class
- Implements Deque
- Uses a dynamic array internally
- Can be used as Queue or Stack
- Preferred in modern Java

Example:
Deque<Integer> dq = new ArrayDeque<>();

Queue Style:
offer()
poll()
peek()

Stack Style:
push()
pop()
peek()

----------------------------------------

Hierarchy:

Collection
   │
   └── Queue (Interface)
          │
          └── Deque (Interface)
                 │
                 ├── ArrayDeque
                 └── LinkedList

Stack (Class)
   │
   └── extends Vector

----------------------------------------

Memory Trick:

Queue      = FIFO
Stack      = LIFO
Deque      = Queue + Stack (Interface)
ArrayDeque = Implementation of Deque

----------------------------------------

Time Complexity:

Queue:
offer() O(1)
poll()  O(1)
peek()  O(1)

Stack:
push()  O(1)
pop()   O(1)
peek()  O(1)

ArrayDeque:
offer() O(1)
poll()  O(1)
push()  O(1)
pop()   O(1)
peek()  O(1)
-----------------------------------------------

conclsuion :

use Deque<Integer> d = new ArrayDeque()<>;

-can do queue
-can do stack
-can do both

Instead of using only linkedList (implimentation) for stack
Instead of using only linkedList (implimentation) for deque

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
In Deque
For a Stack & queue , use the stack-specific & queue-sepcefic methods better understand to reader:

push() -> insert not addLast
pop()  -> remove not removeLast
peek() -> top element not peekLast

Queue Methods
offer() -> insert at rear not addFirst
poll()  -> remove from front not removeFirst
peek()  -> view front not peekFirst